 "result_text": "`validate_regex` in `tavern/testutils/helpers.py` now takes an optional `in_jmespath` argument. I haven't run it or any tests.\n\nWith it set, the regex is matched against the value at that JMES path in the JSON body, instead of the whole response text. Because it's an external function, it runs alongside the normal `json` body validation and doesn't replace it. To check several fields, call it once per field. The version-number case from the issue would be an `ext` call to `tavern.testutils.helpers:validate_regex` with `in_jmespath: version` and `expression: '[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+'`.\n\nIf the value at the path isn't a string (including when the path matches nothing), it fails with an `AssertionError` saying so. If `header` is also given, `header` takes precedence and `in_jmespath` is ignored.\n\nI didn't add tests or update the docs.",
